    "done_when": "Reported by nova-f5: overnight the follower printed 'producer nova runs older code than this follower ... cycle it with: reckon crew unwatch ... && reckon crew watch --ensure' about six times, each right after main moved, and the operator cycled by hand each time. The producer already re-execs itself in place when the code stamp changes (reckon/cli.py, prepare_watch_seat_reexec then os.execve). s21-fin's follower logs show the reckon producer's stamp catching up one merge later. The warning (reckon/cli.py, near the 'cycle it with' text) therefore fires inside the window in which the producer is about to reload itself. The warning fires only once the producer's stamp has stayed behind for longer than its reload window. Until then the follower shows at most a one-line note that the producer is reloading. tests/test_stale_producer_warning_waits_for_its_reload.py drives a seat whose stamp lags for less than the window, with no cycle advice, and for longer, where the cycle advice appears. The declared negative control is executed and logged. Base and head arms of tests/test_follower_checks_its_owner.py and tests/test_producer_holds_a_lease.py show zero added failures.",
    "estimated_hours": 0.8,
    "goal": "The follower warns of a stale producer only when the producer has not reloaded itself within its reload window",
